## npm dependencies

`package-lock.json` is mandatory and CI installs with `npm ci`. Direct production and development packages must appear in `security/approved-dependencies.yml`. Adding a production dependency requires architecture and security review; adding any package requires license, maintenance, permissions, transitive-risk, and bundle-impact review.

## GitHub Actions

Every external Action is listed in `security/approved-actions.yml`, pinned to a verified full 40-character commit SHA, and annotated in workflow source with the reviewed release. Mutable tags and unapproved actions fail workflow validation. Pins are reviewed quarterly and when Dependabot proposes a change.

## Vulnerabilities

Production-reachable critical and high findings block merge. A development-only high finding requires a recorded, expiring exception and isolation evidence. Moderate findings require remediation or a recorded exception. Reports must not publish secrets, environment values, dependency credentials, or PII.

## Current evidence limitation

The dependency installation on 2026-07-27 reported nine moderate and one high transitive vulnerability across the Excalidraw Animate development tree. `npm audit --omit=dev` reported zero production vulnerabilities. npm's suggested fix is a breaking downgrade of the requested viewer, so SEC-DEP-001 records a development-only exception through 2026-08-26. Trusted repository scenes are the only accepted input and the full scheduled audit remains intentionally visible.
